since i began studying higher education  i've seen a lot of myths about student  debt let's dispel  three of them myth number one federal  student loans are only used by  low-income people to afford  college in fact the most well-off  households take on the highest levels of  student debt  that's because they attend expensive  colleges stay in school longer for  graduate and professional degrees  and they use low-cost government  financing over paying with cash  myth number two unaffordable student  debt is inescapable  since 2009 the federal government has  allowed borrowers to reduce their  monthly payments to an amount that's  affordable relative to their income  creating an effective safety net myth  number three  high balances are the norm while the  media tells horror stories about  white-collar professionals  struggling with loan repayment the vast  majority of borrowers have small  balances  and reasonable payments relative to  their income there is room for  improvement in the current system  but misunderstandings should be  clarified so that we don't encourage  support for illogical  or misplaced policies what do you think  needs to be improved  let us know in our poll also let us know  what other topics you'd like us to cover  in 60 seconds  and be sure to like and subscribe for  more research and videos from aei
 

